### MULTILINGUAL STRINGS - NO HARDCODED TEXT

**ALL blade templates MUST be multilingual.** Hardcoded strings in ANY language (Italian, English, etc.) are forbidden.

**WRONG (Hardcoded Italian):**
```blade
<h2>Quanto sono chiare le informazioni?</h2>
<button>Invia</button>
<p>Grazie per il tuo feedback!</p>
<span class="sr-only">Valuta 5 stelle su 5</span>
```

**WRONG (Hardcoded English):**
```blade
<h2>How clear is the information?</h2>
<button>Submit</button>
<p>Thank you for your feedback!</p>
<span class="sr-only">Rate 5 stars out of 5</span>
```

**CORRECT (Translation namespace pattern):**
```blade
@php
    $ns = 'fixcity::rating';
    $title = $data['title'] ?? __($ns . '.title');
@endphp
<h2>{{ $title }}</h2>
<button>{{ __($ns . '.buttons.submit') }}</button>
<p>{{ __($ns . '.thank_you') }}</p>
<span class="sr-only">{{ __($ns . '.star.labels.5') }}</span>
```

**Translation File Structure:**
- Location: `laravel/Modules/Fixcity/lang/{locale}/rating.php`
- Namespace pattern: `fixcity::rating.title`
- Format: `namespace::context.collection.element.type` (5 livelli, SEMPRE!)
- Supported locales: `it`, `en` (minimum)

**Translation Key Pattern Examples:**
- ✅ `fixcity::rating.fields.title.label`
- ✅ `fixcity::rating.fields.star.labels.5`
- ✅ `fixcity::rating.actions.submit.label`
- ✅ `fixcity::segnalazione.heading.title.label`
- ✅ `fixcity::segnalazione.fields.address.label`
- ❌ `fixcity::rating.title` (manca `.collection.`!)
- ❌ `fixcity::rating.star.labels.5` (manca `.collection.`!)
- ❌ `SEGNALAZIONE::SEGNALAZIONE.ELENCO.TITLE` (namespace uppercase)
- ❌ `fixcity::segnalazione.heading.title_label` (underscore invece di dot)

**CORRECT Translation Format (5 levels):**
```php
// fixcity::segnalazione.fields.title.label
return [
    'segnalazione' => [    // context
        'fields' => [      // collection
            'title' => [   // element
                'label' => 'Titolo Segnalazione',  // type
            ],
        ],
    ],
];
```

**Helper Pattern for JSON-driven content:**
```php
$t = function (?string $value, string $fallbackKey) use ($ns): string {
    if (empty($value)) {
        return __($ns . '.' . $fallbackKey);
    }
    if (str_contains($value, '::')) {
        return __($value);
    }
    return $value;
};
```

